# Text is LF in the repository and in every checkout, whatever the platform's git is configured to
# do. Windows runners check out with core.autocrlf on, and CRLF breaks things that compare bytes or
# run scripts: the golden corpora's snapshots, rustfmt's `newline_style = "Unix"`, the generated
# bindings' diff, the `#!/bin/sh` hook fixtures and `gradlew`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The one file Windows itself has to read.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# The pact-specification test cases are the oracle the legacy compiler is checked against, kept
# byte for byte as they were copied (two of them are CRLF upstream).
engine/kernel/tests/fixtures/spec_testcases/** -text
